{"architectures":["x64"],"id":"PowerUserZ.OpenTokenUsage","latestVersion":"0.8.6","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"copyright":"Copyright (c) PowerUserZ","description":"Track all your AI coding subscription usage from the Windows system tray.","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/poweruserz/OpenTokenUsage/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"copyright":"Copyright (c) PowerUserZ","description":"Track all your AI coding subscription usage from the Windows system tray.","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/poweruserz/OpenTokenUsage/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"OpenTokenUsage is a lightweight system-tray app that tracks how much of your AI coding subscriptions you've used (Claude, Codex, Copilot, Cursor, Gemini, and more) in one place. It is a Windows fork of OpenUsage with full Windows support, a plugin-based provider system, and a local HTTP usage API.","moniker":"opentokenusage","name":"OpenTokenUsage","packageUrl":"https://github.com/PowerUserZ/OpenTokenUsage","publisher":"PowerUserZ","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/PowerUserZ/OpenTokenUsage/issues","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/PowerUserZ","releaseNotes":"Muse Code joins the providers, for those who turn it on.\nNew Features\n- Muse Code (Meta): the 5-hour session and weekly limits with their resets and your plan, read from the Muse CLI's login (muse login). It stays off until you turn it on in Settings, and the first-start check never turns it on: its usage comes from the endpoint Meta also uses to hand out the account's API key, so the app asks it at most once every 5 minutes and keeps nothing of that answer but the plan and the limits. While Meta leaves a limit out (an idle 5-hour window), the card keeps the last reading until it resets. Thanks to @yuuta0331 for testing the endpoint on Windows (#88, #92)\nBug Fixes\n- The response log no longer keeps part of a name or other private value that contains a quotation mark (#92)","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/poweruserz/OpenTokenUsage/releases/tag/v0.8.6","tags":["ai","claude","codex","copilot","cursor","developer-tools","gemini","system-tray","usage"]}},"longDescription":"OpenTokenUsage is a lightweight system-tray app that tracks how much of your AI coding subscriptions you've used (Claude, Codex, Copilot, Cursor, Gemini, and more) in one place. It is a Windows fork of OpenUsage with full Windows support, a plugin-based provider system, and a local HTTP usage API.","moniker":"opentokenusage","name":"OpenTokenUsage","packageUrl":"https://github.com/PowerUserZ/OpenTokenUsage","publisher":"PowerUserZ","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/PowerUserZ/OpenTokenUsage/issues","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/PowerUserZ","releaseNotes":"Muse Code joins the providers, for those who turn it on.\nNew Features\n- Muse Code (Meta): the 5-hour session and weekly limits with their resets and your plan, read from the Muse CLI's login (muse login). It stays off until you turn it on in Settings, and the first-start check never turns it on: its usage comes from the endpoint Meta also uses to hand out the account's API key, so the app asks it at most once every 5 minutes and keeps nothing of that answer but the plan and the limits. While Meta leaves a limit out (an idle 5-hour window), the card keeps the last reading until it resets. Thanks to @yuuta0331 for testing the endpoint on Windows (#88, #92)\nBug Fixes\n- The response log no longer keeps part of a name or other private value that contains a quotation mark (#92)","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/poweruserz/OpenTokenUsage/releases/tag/v0.8.6","tags":["ai","claude","codex","copilot","cursor","developer-tools","gemini","system-tray","usage"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/0.8.6/app.json","detailSha256":"47d2d2672ffed26b49ac6cea214fabdf97133cca05a332d8f11f62d02402644b","releaseDate":"2026-11-13","releas